# Alert

A persistent in-page banner stating the current state of the page or
its data, coloured by severity.

<%= embed :alert, :playground %>

## When to use

- Page or data state the user needs while working: "Results are
  more than 24 hours old", "Allergy information could not be
  loaded".
- The error summary at the top of a failed form (see *Forms*).

## When not to use

- Action outcomes — `toast` (see *Feedback*: state persists, outcomes
  expire).
- One record's state in a list — `badge`.
- Empty states — calm body text, not an alert (see *Content*).

## Usage

`render_alert` (`Gesso::Components::AlertHelper`) validates the variant and
renders the component; the block is the alert body.

```erb
<%%= render_alert(title: "Results are stale") do %>
  Results are more than 24 hours old. Refresh to re-check.
<%% end %>
```

Pass a `variant`, an `icon`, and any option below in the same call:

```erb
<%%= render_alert(variant: "warning", icon: "icons/alert-triangle", title: "Caution") do %>
  Proceed with care.
<%% end %>
```

## Variants

<%= embed :alert, :variants %>

| Variant | When to use |
| ------- | ----------- |
| `default` | Neutral information with no state meaning. |
| `info` | Context the reader should note; nothing is wrong. |
| `warning` | Needs attention but isn't an error or blocking. |
| `critical` | A serious clinical or safety state needing action — the strongest signal on a page. |
| `destructive` | A failure, error, or destructive consequence. |

## Options

| Param | Default | Notes |
| ----- | ------- | ----- |
| `variant` | `default` | see **Variants** above |
| `icon` | — | logical icon path, e.g. `"icons/info"` |
| `title` | — | the state, stated plainly |
| `classes` | — | extra CSS classes |

Clinical variants layer token colour onto basecoat's alert layout
(`alert.css`).

## Do and don't

- Do match variant to meaning, not emphasis: `warning` = risk,
  `critical` = harm or blockage, `info` = neutral context (see
  *Colour*).
- Do use the established icon pairings — `alert-triangle` warning,
  `alert-circle` critical, `info` info (see *Icons*).
- Do remove the alert when the state resolves — a stale alert
  trains users to ignore all alerts.
- Don't stack alerts; two states worth announcing usually mean one
  alert summarising and detail in the page.
- Don't make alerts dismissible if the state persists — hiding the
  message doesn't resolve the state.

## Accessibility and content

- State + consequence + action where one exists: "Results are more
  than 24 hours old. Refresh to re-check." (see *Content* for tone).
- Severity is carried by the title text, not only the colour — the
  message must work in greyscale.
- The icon is decorative beside the title; no alt text needed.
